        "type": "the-purpose",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This set of topics explores Cognitive Load Theory (CLT) from a strategic, practical perspective. The central goal is to move beyond a simple academic definition of CLT and frame it as a powerful tool for a self-directed learner. These topics investigate the mechanisms of human cognitive architecture—working memory, schemas, and the three load types—and directly apply these principles to the design of a Personal Knowledge Base (PKB) in a tool like Obsidian. The inquiry also extends to how managing cognitive load is a core component of effective self-development and metacognition, providing a framework for optimizing the entire process of personal growth and skill acquisition.",
        "line_number": 35,
        "source": "topic-set_cognitive-load-theory-for-self-directed-learning-and-personal-knowledge-management_🆔20251109164228.md",
