      "unordered": [
        {
          "text": "**Schema Theory:** This is the other half of the CLT equation. Understanding *how* schemas are formed, organized, and automated is critical.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 108,
          "source": "topic-set_cognitive-load-theory-for-self-directed-learning-and-personal-knowledge-management_🆔20251109164228.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Dual Coding Theory (Paivio):** This pairs perfectly with the \"modality effect\" and \"split-attention effect,\" offering a framework for how to effectively combine text and visuals in your notes.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 108,
          "source": "topic-set_cognitive-load-theory-for-self-directed-learning-and-personal-knowledge-management_🆔20251109164228.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Spaced Repetition & Interleaving:** These are retrieval-practice techniques that directly relate to managing cognitive load over *time* to build robust, long-term schemas.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 112,
          "source": "topic-set_cognitive-load-theory-for-self-directed-learning-and-personal-knowledge-management_🆔20251109164228.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Zone of Proximal Development (Vygotsky):** While from a different tradition (sociocultural), this concept of a \"sweet spot\" for learning maps directly onto the idea of managing *intrinsic load*—keeping tasks difficult enough to be germane, but not so difficult as to be overwhelming.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 115,
          "source": "topic-set_cognitive-load-theory-for-self-directed-learning-and-personal-knowledge-management_🆔20251109164228.md"
        }
      ]
    },
